# /refunds, retired 2026-08-16. It existed for one reason: Paddle's account
# review wants policy URLs on the seller's own domain, and perch was the thing
# that was going to be sold. perch went back to MIT with no paid tier on
# 2026-08-15 (hausfold/perch#67), and the user's decision the next day is that
# hausfold is not selling anything, ever — so the page described a fourteen-day
# refund window for a licence that will never exist.
#
# Unlike every other retirement in this file, it has no successor page: no
# surface here carries what it carried, because what it carried is gone. It
# lands on `/#made`, the "What we make" paragraph, which is where the
# answer now lives ("All of it is free and open source: ... nothing to buy").
# That sentence and that id were added in the same commit for exactly
# this reason — a redirect onto a page that doesn't answer the question is a
# soft 404, and bare `/` would leave the answer below the fold.
# ⚠️ The id was `#apps` until 2026-08-17, when the landing page became the
# house's index and the section stopped being only apps. 🚨 These two lines
# are its only callers, so renaming it again means editing them again.
#
# It was published from 2026-08-08 and linked from /perch's colophon, and a
# policy URL outlives the policy, so it keeps resolving forever.
#
# 🚨 /terms was retired in the same commit and came BACK on 2026-09-04, as
# `src/app/terms/page.tsx`. Its two lines were deleted from here in the same
# commit that added the page, because this file is evaluated AHEAD of the
# assets: a page under a live redirect never renders, whatever the route says.
# That is not a reversal of the decision above. The retired page sold
# something (seats, renewals, that refund window); the new one is
# no-warranty terms of use for a free, keyless, read-only public API,
# written because app-directory submissions require a terms URL and a 301
# onto a landing-page paragraph is a soft 404 in that field. /refunds stays
# retired, because there is still nothing to buy and so nothing to refund.
/refunds    /#made  301
/refunds/   /#made  301

